{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "Me1OHru4vr", "broadcast_date": "2004-07-23", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 760615, "segment_id": "wPBjGhyOIK", "segment_broadcast_id": "Me1OHru4vr", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Peter Jennings (New York)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 50, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 760615, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "Me1OHru4vr", "broadcast_date": "2004-07-23", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 760615, "segment_id": "jxdhvv645O", "segment_broadcast_id": "Me1OHru4vr", "segment_title": "September 11 / Commission Report / Recommendations", "segment_description": "(Studio: Peter Jennings)  The promises to consider the recommendations of the commission that investigated the attacks on September 11 introduced. \n (White House: John Cochran)  The White House reaction featured; details given of the commission's recommendations, including naming an intelligence czar & setting up a national counterterrorism center.  [White House counterterrorism adviser Frances TOWNSEND&#134;- says President Bush is committed to intelligence reform.]  [Former counterterrorism official Richard CLARKE&#134;- says the president could put 90 percent of the commission's suggestions into effect.] \n (Studio: Peter Jennings)  The criticism of the Congress in the report noted. \n (Capitol Hill: Linda Douglass)  The reaction of Congress, which has adjourned for six weeks, to the 9/11 report examined.  [Senator Joseph LIEBERMAN&nbsp- states what the folks back home will ask.]  [9/11 commission member Slade GORTON&#134;- says we'll know who to blame now for not acting.]  [Yesterday, Speaker of the House Dennis HASTERT&#134;&#134;; voters Nina VANDERWAY&#134;, Michael BISHOP&#134;, Senator Susan COLLINS&nbsp- offer differing opinions on the urgency to act.]  The pressure on members of Congress to return in August to hold hearings noted. \n (Studio: Peter Jennings)  Bush's message to the National Urban League noted.  [In speech, BUSH&nbsp- asks if the Democratic Party takes African-American voters for granted.]", "segment_duration": 250, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63050.0", "legacy_segment_id": 760616, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "Me1OHru4vr", "broadcast_date": "2004-07-23", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 760615, "segment_id": "qH2UeSolq5", "segment_broadcast_id": "Me1OHru4vr", "segment_title": "Iraq / Hostages, Attacks / Custer Interview", "segment_description": "(Studio: Peter Jennings)  Al Jazeera report that extremists in Iraq have kidnapped an Egyptian diplomat noted; video shown; details given of the death of two American soldiers near Samarra. \n (Pentagon: Martha Raddatz)  ABCNews exclusive interview held with Central Command senior intelligence director Brig. Gen. John Custer about suicide bombers in Iraq.  [CUSTER&nbsp- says we have found bombers chained to their vehicles; states the role of the foreign fighters is a myth.]  Concern with an increase of violence by Abu Mussab al-Zarqawi as elections in Iraq near noted.  [CUSTER&nbsp- calls Zarqawi \"the rock star terrorist\"; doubts there is a lot of Al Qaeda in Iraq.] \n (Studio: Peter Jennings)  Collision in the Persian Gulf of a Navy vessel, the USS John F. Kennedy, with a small boat reported; map shown.", "segment_duration": 180, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63300.0", "legacy_segment_id": 760617, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "Me1OHru4vr", "broadcast_date": "2004-07-23", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 760615, "segment_id": "ElQS1n8GsX", "segment_broadcast_id": "Me1OHru4vr", "segment_title": "Reagan Voyage", "segment_description": "(Studio: Peter Jennings)  The inaugural voyage of the aircraft carrier the USS Ronald Reagan reported; scenes shown of the ship in San Diego.  [Former First Lady Nancy REAGAN&nbsp- says she is honored to be here.]", "segment_duration": 30, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63480.0", "legacy_segment_id": 760618, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "Me1OHru4vr", "broadcast_date": "2004-07-23", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 760615, "segment_id": "FezeNeXpU1", "segment_broadcast_id": "Me1OHru4vr", "segment_title": "Upcoming Items (Studio: Peter Jennings)", "segment_description": "null", "segme